title: 'statement-store: metrics for the v2 DHT rollout'
doc:
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      Adds metrics to help watch the statement store while some nodes run the new v2 DHT mode
      and others don't yet.

      These metrics now have a `route` label (`dht` or `legacy`). `legacy` covers every
      peer this node sends everything to: v1 peers, v2 peers that sent no filter in time, and all
      peers when the node runs without the v2 DHT. Names stay the same, so dashboards that
      read them without labels may need a `sum()`:
      - `substrate_sync_propagated_statements`
      - `substrate_sync_statements_received`
      - `substrate_sync_statement_bytes_sent_total`
      - `substrate_sync_statement_bytes_received_total`
      - `substrate_sync_initial_sync_statements_sent`
      - `substrate_sync_initial_sync_bursts_total`

      New metrics:
      - `substrate_sync_statement_peers_assumed_match_all_total`: v2 peers that did not send
        their filter in time.
      - `substrate_sync_statement_late_affinity_filters_total`: peers whose filter arrived late.
      - `substrate_sub_statement_store_bytes_by_retention`: bytes in the store per retention track.
crates:
  - name: sc-network-statement
    bump: patch
  - name: sc-statement-store
    bump: patch
